<edge_case_handling>
| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Diff too large to process | Break down by directory; run sequential breadth passes |
| Logic too complex to evaluate | Ask user for narrative context on specific file |
| Contract has_changes is false | Surface contract's reason to user and stop |
| Filtered file count is 0 | Surface that only generated/vendor files changed and stop |
| Both wt_changes and ahead_count are 0 | Surface "No changes" — nothing to review |
| PRD/Constitution missing | Flag as "Governance Gap"; proceed with standard domains |
| Pre-script fails | Surface the failure reason (from stderr/exit code) to user and stop |
</edge_case_handling>

<constraints>
- Execute security and idiomatic analysis for every reviewed artifact.
- Suggest remediation before presenting the problem.
- Include line numbers in all findings.
- Categorize findings strictly by the defined schema.
- Prioritize critical security and architectural violations.
- Refrain from meta-commentary about the review process.
- Ensure all remediations are idiomatic to the target stack.
- When committing review-driven fixes, follow `CONTRIBUTING.md` if present; never invent a conflicting format.
</constraints>
